{
  "concept": "Reinforcement learning is a closed loop: the environment hands the agent a state and reward, the agent's policy turns that state into an action, and the environment's transition and reward functions produce the next state and reward — one MDP time step.",
  "figureType": "diagram",
  "elements": [
    "Upper rounded rectangle, light teal fill with dark outline, title 'Agent'",
    "Inside Agent box: 'Policy π[a_t|s_t]'",
    "Lower, larger rounded rectangle, light teal fill with dark outline, title 'Environment'",
    "Inside Environment box: 'State transition' with 'Pr(s_{t+1}|s_t, a_t)'",
    "Inside Environment box: 'Reward function' with 'Pr(r_{t+1}|s_t, a_t)'",
    "Orange arrow: Agent → right side → down → into Environment right edge (action a_t)",
    "Orange arrow: Environment right edge (lower) ← from far-right vertical path (reward channel routing)",
    "Orange arrow: state path leaving Environment left edge at s_{t+1}, routing left and up into Agent left edge (labeled State s_t)",
    "Orange arrow: reward path leaving Environment left edge at r_{t+1}, routing far left and up into Agent top-left edge (labeled Reward r_t)",
    "Orange arrow: inner return path from Environment area up to Agent second input (State s_t)",
    "Vertical dashed black line on the left of the Environment box representing the one-step time delay",
    "Labels on the dashed line: 's_{t+1}' (upper) and 'r_{t+1}' (lower), each on a white background chip",
    "Left-side outside labels on white chips: 'Reward r_t' and 'State s_t'",
    "Right-side outside labels on white chips: 'State s_t' and 'Action a_t'",
    "Arrowheads (orange, solid) at every path terminus"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "stepCycle",
      "type": "animation",
      "label": "Play one MDP time step",
      "loop": true,
      "teaches": "The strict temporal order of a single RL time step: observe state and reward → choose action → environment responds with next state and reward, which become the next step's inputs."
    },
    {
      "id": "focusBox",
      "type": "click",
      "teaches": "Clicking the Agent highlights the policy π[a_t|s_t] and the outgoing action arrow (the agent's only output); clicking the Environment highlights the state-transition and reward-function distributions and their outgoing s_{t+1}/r_{t+1} arrows (the environment's only outputs)."
    },
    {
      "id": "phase",
      "type": "state",
      "label": "Loop phase",
      "states": ["idle", "observe", "act", "respond", "advance"],
      "default": "idle",
      "teaches": "Each phase of the loop can be visited deliberately, separating what the agent knows (s_t, r_t) from what the environment computes (s_{t+1}, r_{t+1})."
    },
    {
      "id": "timeShift",
      "type": "toggle",
      "label": "Show time delay (dashed line)",
      "default": true,
      "teaches": "The dashed line is a one-step delay: the environment's outputs s_{t+1} and r_{t+1} are relabeled s_t and r_t when they arrive at the agent on the next tick."
    }
  ],
  "demo_steps": [
    {
      "title": "The closed loop",
      "narration": "Two components only: an Agent holding a policy, and an Environment holding a state-transition and a reward distribution. Every orange arrow is information passing between them.",
      "state": { "phase": "idle", "timeShift": true }
    },
    {
      "title": "Agent observes s_t and r_t",
      "narration": "The environment's last outputs arrive at the agent as the current state s_t and reward r_t — these are the agent's only inputs.",
      "state": { "phase": "observe", "timeShift": true }
    },
    {
      "title": "Policy chooses a_t",
      "narration": "The policy π[a_t|s_t] maps the observed state to an action a_t, which travels around the right side into the environment.",
      "state": { "phase": "act", "timeShift": true }
    },
    {
      "title": "Environment responds",
      "narration": "Given s_t and a_t, the environment samples the next state from Pr(s_{t+1}|s_t,a_t) and the reward from Pr(r_{t+1}|s_t,a_t) — both outputs depend only on the current state and action, which is the Markov property.",
      "state": { "phase": "respond", "timeShift": true }
    },
    {
      "title": "Time advances",
      "narration": "Crossing the dashed line, s_{t+1} and r_{t+1} become s_t and r_t for the next tick, and the identical cycle repeats forever.",
      "state": { "phase": "advance", "timeShift": true }
    },
    {
      "title": "Hide the delay",
      "narration": "Without the dashed delay line the diagram looks like simultaneous exchange — the delay is what makes it a sequential decision process rather than a single function evaluation.",
      "state": { "phase": "advance", "timeShift": false }
    }
  ],
  "keyInsight": "The agent's only output is an action and the environment's only outputs are a next state and a reward — and because those outputs depend on nothing but the current state and action, the whole of reinforcement learning is this one Markov loop repeated.",
  "keyInsightNote": "",
  "reconstructionNotes": "Two rounded rectangles on a white background, both filled light teal (#9ed8cd) with a dark charcoal outline and black serif/math text. The Agent box sits upper-center-right and is smaller; the Environment box sits lower-center and is taller, holding two stacked captions ('State transition' over Pr(s_{t+1}|s_t,a_t), and 'Reward function' over Pr(r_{t+1}|s_t,a_t)). All connector paths are salmon/orange (#d9805c), orthogonal (right-angle elbows) with solid triangular arrowheads. Two paths enter the Agent's left edge (upper = Reward r_t from the far-left channel, lower = State s_t from an inner channel); two paths leave the Agent's right edge and descend the right side to enter the Environment's right edge (upper arrow = state routing, lower = action a_t). On the Environment's left edge, two short stubs exit toward a bold vertical dashed black line, tagged 's_{t+1}' above and 'r_{t+1}' below on white chips. Outside variable labels sit in the wide empty band between the boxes, on white chips so arrows appear broken behind them: 'Reward r_t' and 'State s_t' on the left, 'State s_t' and 'Action a_t' on the right. Highlighting should brighten the active path to a saturated orange with a thicker stroke and dim inactive paths to pale gray; box focus adds a glow/outline to the box and bolds its inner math."
}

